cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tri Language findings, please cite this work. Linear types, algebraic effects, dual-target codegen to Zig/Verilog."
title: "Trinity B005: Tri Language — Linear Types, Algebraic Effects, Dual-Target Codegen"
abstract: "We present Tri Language, a domain-specific language for ternary computing with advanced type system features and dual-target code generation. Key innovations include: (1) Linear Types + Ownership (Let/Inout/Sink/Set modes) for resource-safe compilation; (2) Algebraic Effects + Handlers with platform-aware effect resolution; (3) Bit/Trit Pattern Matching at hardware level; (4) Content-Addressed Functions via SHA256 AST hashing; (5) Result Type (Austral-style error handling); (6) Array Combinators (map/filter/reduce); (7) Pipe Operator for chaining operations; (8) Dual-Target Codegen generating both Zig (for CPU) and Verilog (for FPGA) from single .tri spec. The language enables zero-cost abstractions for ternary computing while maintaining memory safety and eliminating runtime exceptions. Pure Zig implementation with VIBEE compiler infrastructure. Complete language reference with grammar specification, type system formalization, and compilation pipeline."
